## 2. Sovereign Speed Strategy — The Fix Architecture

### 2.1 — The Three Tiers of Sovereign Acceleration

Per Python Unleashed and Sovereign Integration Guide, we have three acceleration tiers:

| Tier | Method | Speedup | When to Use |
|------|--------|---------|-------------|
| **Tier 1: ctypes C-library calls** | Call existing C functions (zlib, OpenSSL) via ctypes | 20–50x | BWT sort, Huffman codec, SHA-256 |
| **Tier 2: Assembly injection** | Sovereign.allocate_executable() + hand-written x86-64 | 50–200x | LZ77 match finding, MTF encode, bit-packing |
| **Tier 3: Compiled EXE** | ETPL/Cython/Nuitka compilation to native binary | 100–500x | Entire compressor as standalone binary |

### 2.2 — Tier 1 Strategy: ctypes C Library Bindings (IMMEDIATE)

**These require ZERO new math derivations — just rewiring to existing C libraries already on the system.**

| Hot Path | C Library | Function | Expected Speedup |
|----------|-----------|----------|-----------------|
| BWT suffix sort | `ctypes.cdll.LoadLibrary("msvcrt")` / libc | `qsort()` with custom comparator via ctypes callback | 20–40x |
| SHA-256 hashing | `hashlib` (already C-backed) | Already using it — but eliminate redundant calls | 2–3x |
| Huffman bit-packing | `struct.pack` / manual `int` ops | Replace string bit manipulation with integer arithmetic | 10–30x |
| Memory copies | `ctypes.memmove` | Fix `_fast_copy` to avoid intermediate allocations | 3–5x |
| zlib baseline | `zlib.compress` | Use as fallback/comparison — already C-speed | baseline |

### 2.3 — Tier 2 Strategy: Sovereign Assembly Injection (MEDIUM TERM)

**These require new ET math derivations for the injection descriptors.**

| Hot Path | Assembly Operation | Registers | New Eq Needed |
|----------|-------------------|-----------|---------------|
| LZ77 match extend | `repe cmpsb` (string compare) | rsi=src, rdi=dest, rcx=max_len | Eq 236 |
| MTF encode | Lookup table with `xlat` | rbx=table_base, al=byte | Eq 237 |
| Bit-pack Huffman | `bts`/`btr` bit manipulation | rax=accumulator, rcx=bit_pos | Eq 238 |
| Delta encode | SIMD `psubb` (packed byte subtract) | xmm0=current, xmm1=previous | Eq 239 |
| RLE scan | `repe scasb` (repeat scan) | rdi=data, al=byte, rcx=max | Eq 240 |

### 2.4 — Tier 3 Strategy: Full EXE Compilation (LONG TERM)

**Options for compiling the entire compressor to native code:**

| Method | Tool | Speedup | Complexity | Notes |
|--------|------|---------|------------|-------|
| **PyInstaller + ctypes hot paths** | PyInstaller | 1.5–2x (packaging only) | Low | Doesn't speed up Python itself |
| **Nuitka** | Nuitka compiler | 3–8x | Medium | Compiles Python to C, then to EXE |
| **Cython** | Cython + gcc/MSVC | 10–50x (hot paths) | Medium | .pyx files for hot functions only |
